---

!! Real-world example: E-commerce order domain model

This example models an e-commerce domain with entities grouped by stereotype: value objects, aggregate roots, services, and repositories. Each group uses a `classDef` category so the legend maps colors to domain roles.

```
classDiagram
    accTitle: E-commerce order domain model
    accDescr: Domain model showing entities, stereotypes, and relationships

    %% ── Value objects ───────────────────────────
    class Money {
        +float amount
        +String currency
        +add(Money) Money
    }
    class Address {
        +String street
        +String city
        +String country
    }

    %% ── Aggregate roots ─────────────────────────
    class Order {
        +String id
        +OrderStatus status
        +List~OrderItem~ items
        +Money total
        +place()
        +cancel()
        +ship()
    }
    class Customer {
        +String id
        +String email
        +List~Order~ orders
        +register()
    }
    class Product {
        +String id
        +String name
        +Money price
        +int stock
    }

    %% ── Supporting classes ───────────────────────
    class OrderItem {
        +int quantity
        +Money lineTotal
    }
    class OrderStatus {
        <<enumeration>>
        PENDING
        CONFIRMED
        SHIPPED
        DELIVERED
        CANCELLED
    }

    %% ── Services and repositories ────────────────
    class OrderService {
        <<service>>
        +createOrder(Customer, List~Product~) Order
        +processPayment(Order) bool
    }
    class OrderRepository {
        <<repository>>
        +findById(String) Order
        +save(Order)
        +findByCustomer(Customer) List~Order~
    }

    %% ── Relationships ────────────────────────────
    Customer "1" --> "*" Order : places
    Order "1" *-- "*" OrderItem : contains
    OrderItem "*" --> "1" Product : references
    Order --> Money : total
    Customer --> Address : shippingAddress
    OrderService ..> Order : creates
    OrderService ..> OrderRepository : uses

    %% ── Class definitions ───────────────────────
    classDef valueObject fill:#6f42c1,stroke:#432874,color:#fff
    classDef aggregate   fill:#0d6efd,stroke:#084298,color:#fff
    classDef supporting  fill:#198754,stroke:#0f5132,color:#fff
    classDef service     fill:#fd7e14,stroke:#984c0c,color:#fff

    class Money:::valueObject
    class Address:::valueObject
    class Order:::aggregate
    class Customer:::aggregate
    class Product:::aggregate
    class OrderItem:::supporting
    class OrderStatus:::supporting
    class OrderService:::service
    class OrderRepository:::service
```

