|!Color|!Meaning|
|@@background-color:#6f42c1;color:#fff;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:3px;@@ Value Object|Immutable object defined by its value, not identity|
|@@background-color:#0d6efd;color:#fff;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:3px;@@ Aggregate Root|Entity that owns a consistency boundary|
|@@background-color:#198754;color:#fff;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:3px;@@ Supporting|Helper class within an aggregate|
|@@background-color:#fd7e14;color:#fff;padding:2px 8px;border-radius:3px;@@ Service / Repository|Domain service or persistence abstraction|

---

!! Syntax

```
classDiagram
    class MyClass {
        <<stereotype>>
        +String publicField
        -int privateField
        #bool protectedField
        +publicMethod() ReturnType
        -privateMethod()
    }
    ClassA <|-- ClassB : inherits
    ClassA "1" *-- "*" ClassC : composition
    ClassA --> ClassD : association
    ClassA ..> ClassE : dependency
```

|!Visibility|!Meaning|
|`+`|Public|
|`-`|Private|
|`#`|Protected|
|`~`|Package / internal|

|!Relationship|!Meaning|
|`<|--`|Inheritance|
|`*--`|Composition|
|`o--`|Aggregation|
|`-->`|Association|
|`..>`|Dependency|

!! Tips

* Use `classDiagram` (not the legacy `classDiagram-v2`).
* Use only simple generics like `~List~` — nested generics with commas (`~Map~` is fine, but `~Map<K,V>~` causes a parse error).
* `<<stereotype>>` labels (e.g. `<<enumeration>>`, `<<service>>`, `<<interface>>`) appear as a small italic header inside the class box.
* Apply `classDef` and `:::` to group classes by domain role and pair with a color legend.
* See also: [[Entity Relationship]] for data-centric schemas, [[State Diagram]] for lifecycle modeling.

